     1	#!/usr/bin/env bash
     2	# ============================================================================
     3	# release.sh — operator release driver. Version-neutral BY NAME.
     4	#
     5	# The previous driver carried a release number in its own FILENAME, and was
     6	# still driving the release after that one — the root of a whole class: a
     7	# driver named for one release is a standing invitation for every other version
     8	# literal inside it to go stale too. Everything release-specific now lives in
     9	# the PER-RELEASE block below, and every message derives from it. The old path
    10	# is deliberately left unspelled on every live surface, so the AC-6 control
    11	# needs no "except this one" exemption; `git log --follow` is the archaeology.
    12	#
    13	# Implements the documented procedure in `.github/release-checklist.md`:
    14	# RC first (vX.Y.Z-rc.N), then the ADR-103 24 h hold, then promote stable.
    15	#
    16	# WHAT THE OWNER SIGNS. Nothing here is a canonical-edit ceremony: CHANGELOG.md,
    17	# VERSION and npm/package.json are NOT in `_CANONICAL_GUARDS`
    18	# (`.claude/hooks/check_canonical_edit.py`), so no sentinel `approved.md`
    19	# exists for a release. The Owner signature is the **annotated GPG tag**,
    20	# produced INLINE by the `tag` phase (family lesson: a ceremony script signs
    21	# inline and never demands a pre-existing `.asc`).
    22	#
    23	# WHAT THIS SCRIPT NEVER DOES. It never pushes, and it never publishes.
    24	# Pushing the tag is the irreversible, outward-facing step: it starts BOTH
    25	# `.github/workflows/release.yml` (the release gate) and
    26	# `.github/workflows/npm-publish.yml` — and npm-publish.yml is what actually
    27	# publishes to npm via OIDC. This driver prints the push command and stops.
    28	#
    29	# Phases (run in order):
    30	#   preflight  read-only gates, fail-closed          (default)
    31	#   bump       version sites + plugin manifests + commit
    32	#   tag        annotated GPG tag, signed inline, behind two fail-closed guards
    33	#
    34	# Usage:
    35	#   bash .claude/scripts/local/release.sh preflight
    36	#   bash .claude/scripts/local/release.sh bump --dry-run
    37	#   bash .claude/scripts/local/release.sh bump
    38	#   bash .claude/scripts/local/release.sh tag --dry-run
    39	#   bash .claude/scripts/local/release.sh tag
    40	#
    41	# Options:
    42	#   --dry-run        make no lasting change; restores BOTH working tree and
    43	#                    index on exit (trap), including on failure. The restore
    44	#                    list is DERIVED from _release_bump_sites.py, never typed.
    45	#   --stable         target the bare version instead of -rc.N (post-hold promote)
    46	#   --rc N           RC ordinal (default 1)
    47	#   --key KEYID      GPG key to sign with (default: the key of the last release)
    48	#   --today DATE     YYYY-MM-DD stamped into the `last-reviewed:` lines
    49	#                    (default: today). It exists so the D/D+1 idempotence
    50	#                    invariant is testable at the driver level; it changes only
    51	#                    the stamp date and skips no gate.
    52	#   --restamp        force the four `last-reviewed:` stamps to move even when
    53	#                    the version is unchanged — the named route for a REAL
    54	#                    re-review. Requires --npm-readme-reviewed and disables the
    55	#                    no-op fast path (otherwise it would be dead letter).
    56	#   --offline-ack    ancestry guard: skip the `git fetch` and judge HEAD
    57	#                    against the last-known origin/main (announced loudly)
    58	#   --npm-readme-reviewed
    59	#                    required by `bump` when it writes: acknowledges that
    60	#                    npm/README.md was actually re-read. Its `last-reviewed`
    61	#                    stamp is a release tripwire by design; re-stamping it
    62	#                    silently would defeat the gate.
    63	# ============================================================================
