codex
A coerência nominal dos templates está correta: os dois allowlists incluem exatamente manifesto + basenames + verdict-fields/verdict, e o `parent_sha` coincide com o pai do commit do veredito que o step 15 deriva. Os bloqueadores que restam estão nas transições de estado, não nessa modelagem.
codex
P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-RC3-CUT.sh:229` — Commit 1’s directory allowlist is not closed at staging time. The exact directory checks run before the prompt, signing, pack application, and tests; a regular file added afterward under `repass-rc3-cures/`, `staged-rc3/`, `repass-ga-rc2-NOGO/`, or `staged-w3/` matches the prefix rule and is recursively staged at line 303. Because `parent_sha` is commit 1, neither local nor server delta guards see the extra file. Minimal fix: stage manifest-derived literal paths, then verify cached path and content equality immediately before committing; do not `git add` directory prefixes.

P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-RC3-CUT.sh:239` — A failed `git status` is interpreted as an empty, clean tree because it runs inside a heredoc command substitution. The later untracked check at line 309 also swallows status failures with `|| true`. A staged path outside the allowlist can therefore enter the unrestricted commit at line 311, become the reviewed parent, and escape the delta guard. Minimal fix: capture status output with `status="$(git status ...)" || die`, parse that captured value, and assert the final cached path set before commit.

P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-RC3-CUT.sh:272` — The live-file tri-state hashes through symlinks and ignores Git mode. A canonical path replaced by a symlink to its staged cure hashes as “already applied,” so the copy is skipped and `git add` commits the symlink rather than the reviewed regular file. A wrong executable bit is preserved similarly. Minimal fix: require every live target to be a non-symlink regular file with the expected mode, or always perform the verified temporary-copy-and-rename to normalize type and mode.

P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-GA-CUT.sh:188` — RC/SHA provenance and manifest integrity are validated only when deciding whether to reuse existing evidence, not after executing the runner at line 196. A stale or partially re-pointed runner can review rc.2, return two exact GO verdicts, produce a self-consistent manifest, and proceed toward a signed GA envelope without any post-run assertion that the evidence names rc.3 and `$RC_SHA`. Minimal fix: create one evidence-validation function—manifest verification, exact rc.3 tag/SHA binding, exact `RUNNER-OVERALL: rc=0`, and physical set equality—and call it both before reuse and unconditionally after the runner.

P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-GA-CUT.sh:62` — The local-tag-only recovery explicitly instructs the Owner to push the tag directly. That is exactly the state left after lowercase/non-`SIM` confirmation or interruption after tag creation, so recovery bypasses the ceremony’s literal `SIM` gate and its revalidation path. Minimal fix: retain a `LOCAL_TAG_ONLY` state, verify signature/tag target/main/guard again, and route it through the same exact-`SIM` prompt before pushing.

The template basenames, allowlist set equality, `parent_sha`, and reused inputs hash are otherwise coherent, but these P1 transition holes require another cure round.

